The following code snippet contains a bug:

```php
    public function sometimes($attribute, $rules, callable $callback)
    {
        $payload = new Fluent($this->data);

        foreach ((array) $attribute as $key) {
            $response = (new ValidationRuleParser($this->data))->explode([$key => $rules]);

            foreach ($response->rules as $ruleKey => $ruleValue) {
                if ($callback($payload, $this->dataForSometimesIteration($ruleKey, ! Str::endsWith($key, '.*')))) {
                    $this->addRules([$ruleKey => $ruleValue]);
                }
            }
        }

        return $this;
    }
```

The code fails the following tests:

Test `Illuminate\Tests\Validation\ValidationValidatorTest::testValidateSometimesImplicitEachWithAsterisksBeforeAndAfter`:
            
```php
    public function testValidateSometimesImplicitEachWithAsterisksBeforeAndAfter()
    {
        $trans = $this->getIlluminateArrayTranslator();

        $v = new Validator($trans, [
            'foo' => [
                ['start' => '2016-04-19', 'end' => '2017-04-19'],
            ],
        ], []);
        $v->sometimes('foo.*.start', ['before:foo.*.end'], function () {
            return true;
        });
        $this->assertTrue($v->passes());

        $v = new Validator($trans, [
            'foo' => [
                ['start' => '2016-04-19', 'end' => '2017-04-19'],
            ],
        ], []);
        $v->sometimes('foo.*.start', 'before:foo.*.end', function () {
            return true;
        });
        $this->assertTrue($v->passes());

        $v = new Validator($trans, [
            'foo' => [
                ['start' => '2016-04-19', 'end' => '2017-04-19'],
            ],
        ], []);
        $v->sometimes('foo.*.end', ['before:foo.*.start'], function () {
            return true;
        });

        $this->assertTrue($v->fails());

        $v = new Validator($trans, [
            'foo' => [
                ['start' => '2016-04-19', 'end' => '2017-04-19'],
            ],
        ], []);
        $v->sometimes('foo.*.end', ['after:foo.*.start'], function () {
            return true;
        });
        $this->assertTrue($v->passes());

        $v = new Validator($trans, [
            'foo' => [
                ['start' => '2016-04-19', 'end' => '2017-04-19'],
            ],
        ], []);
        $v->sometimes('foo.*.start', ['after:foo.*.end'], function () {
            return true;
        });
        $this->assertTrue($v->fails());
    }
```

The error message is:

```
Failed asserting that false is true.
```

Please provide a fixed version of the buggy function, and only that function without additional imports. Make sure the code is between ``` and ```.
```php
public function sometimes($attribute, $rules, callable $callback)
{
    $payload = new Fluent($this->data);

    foreach ((array) $attribute as $key) {
        $response = (new ValidationRuleParser($this->data))->explode([$key => $rules]);

        foreach ($response->rules as $ruleKey => $ruleValue) {
            $dots = Str::contains($key, '.*');
            $iterationData = $this->dataForSometimesIteration($ruleKey,!$dots);
            if ($dots) {
                // Handle the case where the attribute contains '.*'
                $baseKey = str_replace('.*', '', $key);
                foreach ($this->data[$baseKey]?? [] as $index => $item) {
                    $iteratedKey = str_replace('.*', ".$index", $ruleKey);
                    $iteratedData = $this->dataForSometimesIteration($iteratedKey, true);
                    if ($callback($payload, $iteratedData)) {
                        $this->addRules([$iteratedKey => $ruleValue]);
                    }
                }
            } else {
                if ($callback($payload, $iterationData)) {
                    $this->addRules([$ruleKey => $ruleValue]);
                }
            }
        }
    }

    return $this;
}
```
